/learn/: the instructor application beside the page; a quieter QR in the hero

Rebased on #360 (the booking planner), with the copy and data edits made beside it.

/learn/
- The page reads down the left (classes, what ran before) while "Teaching at FC Public Media", its
  two paragraphs and the application fill the right from the top; on a phone they stack in order.
- The application sends the site-worker's `instructor` tank. Only email is required: who someone is
  gets sorted out on our side, never theirs. Pairs side by side: name, email/phone, first time and in
  person or online, what you'd teach / why FCPM, years / where, times / days; then anything else.
- "This would be my first time" is a checkbox that sends "Yes"; in person or online is a radio.
  answers.js now reads radio groups (only the checked one) and a checkbox's own value as text.

The hero QR
- Its white tile is translucent (`--qr-light`, 35%) over the glass: the densest thing in the hero stops
  being its brightest, the modules stay solid black, and it still decodes. No blend mode: the panel's
  counter-rotation isolates the lockup, and luminosity cannot tint white.

Copy and data (hand edits)
- `fcpm.email.education`; the street as "200 Mathews St"; /reserve/'s introduction above the studio
  request and "Equipment rental" copy; "Tappable Check-In"; check-in without the staff link; orientation
  out of hosts.yml's supports.

Merge qualifications:
- [x] jekyll build clean on #360 plus this
- [x] Playwright against that build: 476 passed, 3 skipped; reserve 22/22 with the booking planner
- [x] the hero QR decodes at 35% (OpenCV, desktop and phone screenshots)
- [ ] a real phone camera on the hero QR

Carried, not decided:
- The failures left are the ones before this: meet-board (the old /meet/), the home page's contrast and
  hero-video checks, and upload's PyYAML test on the LAN Mac.
- With orientation out of hosts.yml, the kiosk's door no longer lists anyone as helping with orientation.
